  "_harvestedAt": "2026-07-31",
  "_how": "Walked figma.root.children with `await page.loadAsync()` on each - a page's children are unavailable until it is loaded, and skipping that is what produced a false \"seven pages are empty\" reading earlier. Counted COMPONENT_SET children per page and their variants, and read variantGroupProperties for the axis names.",
  "_why_no_set_names": "The 1,799 individual set names are NOT stored. Every one follows the same pattern - \"<Category> / <n> /\" - so a list of them is 1,799 near-identical strings carrying no information the category and count do not already carry. Recording them would be a large artefact that looks like evidence and is not. The naming convention is recorded instead, which is the part that can be checked.",
  "_measured_defect": "One of the 32 Navbar sets declares its variant property as \"Breakpint\" rather than \"Breakpoint\". Every other set in the entire kit uses \"Breakpoint\". Any tooling that switches a section between breakpoints by property NAME will silently fail on that one set, and it is invisible in the canvas.",
  "_workspace": "The kit ships the four-view workspace this programme is adopting, as four dedicated pages: Sitemap, Wireframe, Style Guide, Design. Three of the four are empty in the community file - they are working surfaces, not deliverables - which is itself the point: the views are PROJECTIONS a team fills, not artefacts the library hands over.",
